   "line": 6,
   "text": "Now the dramatic move. A four-sample DFT is a DFT, so split it too, and again, down to single samples, which cost nothing. Only butterflies are left, three layers of four: forty-eight multiplications instead of a hundred and twenty-eight. That's the FFT, the fast Fourier transform.",
