   "line": 7,
   "text": "Back to the line. The FFT halves the block again and again, so its length must be a power of two, and two hundred and five is five times forty-one. Take two hundred and fifty-six: every keypad tone still gets its own bin, and the chip can spend thirty-two thousand a block.",
